// @test: run
// @level: L2
// @tier: 0
// @tags: tensors, shapes
// @timeout: 30000
// @expected-exit: 0
// @expected-stdout: added
// @ignore: no tensor literal survives execution today — measured
//   2026-09-03, `let a = tensor<2, 3> Float32 { };` alone dies with
//   `internal compiler error (worker thread panicked): Expected int, got
//   Some(0)`, with or without a body and with or without arithmetic. A
//   file containing no tensor runs. This file is the control for its
//   sibling AND the pin for that crash.
// @description: Adding tensors of the same shape works — the control
//   without which the sibling's clean result proves nothing.

// If shape checking is ever wired up, a version that refuses EVERYTHING
// would satisfy `shape_mismatch_must_not_reach_the_backend.vr` on its
// own. This file is what stops that.
//
// It also caught an error in the sibling's write-up: that file's first
// version claimed "the same-shape control compiles and runs". The
// control had been verified under `check` and reported under `run`.
// Running it is what produced the ICE above. Two modes are two
// measurements.
//
// T1073.

public fn main() -> Int {
    let a = tensor<2, 3> Float32 { };
    let b = tensor<2, 3> Float32 { };
    let c = a + b;

    print("added");
    0
}
